Interestingly, in a part of the TL passage which I omitted, pc discusses
the 1975 Loglan word for "psychology", which is (in Lojban form)
"trasensi", behave-science.  He criticizes this form as being too specific --
it assumes behaviorism as the dominant form of psychology (probably true
in American academia in 1969, when the first edition of L4/L5 came out).

> A much better term for philosophy would be "mother-of-sciences."

An interesting idea: "skemamta", anyone?  Probably needs to be "pevskemamta",
but that would meet Nick's point about philosophy being idiosyncratic:
use a figurative lujvo rather than a Latinate le'avla.

